.git
.gitignore
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/*.tmp
**/*.orig

# Real Cargo build outputs only (do NOT use broad **/target/ or **/build/
# patterns: vendored crates legitimately ship source under paths such as
# app/vendor/cc/src/target/ and app/vendor/thiserror/build/).
app/target/
**/target/debug/
**/target/release/
**/.fingerprint/
**/incremental/

# NOTE: vendored Rust crates under app/vendor/ legitimately contain
# directories and files named things like "build", "tests", "examples", or
# "output" (e.g. build-script helper sources). Cargo's offline vendor
# verification requires every file recorded in each crate's
# .cargo-checksum.json to actually be present, so excluding any generic
# basename pattern here would silently break `cargo build --offline`. Keep
# exclusions scoped to real siblings of this build context instead of
# generic basenames, and explicitly guard the vendor tree.
!app/vendor/**
